        "original_id": "cd0c93ed-d46c-50ae-87e8-a17ef2794053",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Ilysiakos B.C.\n- People: Antonis Fotsis\n- Places: Ilissia\n- Concepts: Elysium, Greek alphabet, Phoenician alphabet\n- Roles: Professional basketball player\n\nFacts:\n- The Greek alphabet was derived from the earlier Phoenician alphabet.\n- The Greek alphabet was the first alphabetic script to have distinct letters for both vowels and consonants.\n- Antonis Fotsis, also spelled Antonios Fotsis, was born on April 2, 1981.\n- Antonis Fotsis is a Greek professional basketball player for Ilysiakos B.C.\n- Ilysiakos B.C.'s name is said to reference Elysium.\n- Ilysiakos B.C.'s name and logo begin with the Greek letter Η instead of Ι.\n- Ilissia, where Ilysiakos B.C. is based, begins with the Greek letter Ι in Greek.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
